;; Genesis 3. Format: gsb/translation/README.md. Check: make gsb/lint

(note "**Demonstratives and open referents.** The Greek of this chapter often points with αὕτη, \"this [one]\", or leaves the speaker as a bare verb ending (\"he said\", 3:10-11, 16-17). Both layers keep that: αὕτη is never \"she\", and a \"he\" is never replaced by \"Adam\" or \"God\" where the Greek has no name.")

(note "**Sorrow.** The Greek uses one word, λύπη, \"sorrow\", for the woman (3:16) and the man (3:17), as the Hebrew uses one root for both. John 16:21 takes it up: \"the woman, when she gives birth, has sorrow (λύπην)\".")

